# Implementation Plan - Admin Direct Fund Allocation UI

Build a dedicated **Direct Fund Allocation** module allowing Administrators to directly push funds into Manager (and team member) wallets from the Admin Dashboard, recording an atomic ledger transaction and immediately updating the manager's available balance.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend

#### [MODIFY] [fundRequestRoutes.js](file:///d:/EstateSync/backend/src/routes/fundRequestRoutes.js)
- Add `POST /api/v1/fund-requests/allocate` route protected with `verifyJWT` and `checkPermission('fund.allocate')`.

#### [MODIFY] [fundRequestController.js](file:///d:/EstateSync/backend/src/controller/fundRequestController.js)
- Implement `directAllocateFunds`:
  - Validates `targetUserId`, `amount` (> 0), and `description`.
  - Executes a Prisma transaction (`$transaction`):
    1. Increments `totalAllocated` and `availableBalance` on target user's `Wallet`.
    2. Creates an immutable `WalletTransaction` with type `FUND_ALLOCATION`, status `COMPLETED`, and reference `DIRECT_ALLOCATION`.
  - Returns the updated wallet and created transaction.

#### [MODIFY] [userController.js](file:///d:/EstateSync/backend/src/controller/userController.js) & [userRoutes.js](file:///d:/EstateSync/backend/src/routes/userRoutes.js)
- Enhance `getManagers` (or add `getFundableUsers`) to include the user's current wallet balance and role name, so the Admin can see the current balance of each manager directly in the selection dropdown.

---

### Frontend

#### [NEW] [DirectFundAllocationForm.js](file:///d:/EstateSync/frontend/src/components/DirectFundAllocationForm.js)
- Create a dedicated component with:
  - Manager / User dropdown showing Name, Email, and Current Wallet Balance.
  - Amount input field with currency symbol (₹).
  - Reason / Description field.
  - Submit action with loading spinner, success feedback, and form reset.
  - `onAllocationSuccess` callback to refresh the stats and transaction ledger dynamically.

#### [MODIFY] [Admin Dashboard](file:///d:/EstateSync/frontend/src/app/dashboards/admin/page.js)
- Embed `DirectFundAllocationForm` in the Admin Dashboard alongside user registration and stats.

